posts.text:
Pavel Mintyukov (IR - day-to-day, lower-body) is back on the Ducks at practice today.

Another day breaking in the Hometown Remix gear, as well.

@SportingTrib | #FlyTogether

Beckett Sennecke with another bad penalty. High sticking on the forecheck in overtime, and Canucks get their 6th power play of the game.

5-5, 2:11 to play in OT.

@SportingTrib | #FlyTogether

Vancouver ties it. Ducks again can't clear the zone, and their three-goal lead is gone with 1:57 to play.

Dostál can't cover up, and Vancouver fishes it out to the point, where Lekkerimäki scores his second in a minute. 5-5 in Anaheim.

@SportingTrib | #FlyTogether

Ducks are full speed ahead. Leo Carlsson crashes the net to clean up a Jeff Malott rebound off the rush.

4-1 Anaheim, 1:36 P2.

@SportingTrib | #FlyTogether

Ducks go back in front 30 seconds after Vancouver's equalizer. It's a grinders' kind of night, as Jeff Malott finishes off Jackson LaCombe's pass in front.

LaCombe's second assist tonight, 5th in the last 4 games. 2-1 Ducks. 

@SportingTrib | #FlyTogether

Ducks deservedly on the board first, and one hell of a feed by AJ Greer. Spins and fires through a tiny window in front to a crashing Tim Washe.

1-0 Ducks, 4:09 P1.

@SportingTrib | #FlyTogether

This is the first time all season the Ducks have not swapped a scratched player for one in the line-up or due to injury.

Aside from Hinds and Mitchell switching defensive pairs, this is the Ducks' most continuous line-up of the last seven games.

@SportingTrib | #FlyTogether

Ducks tie it right back up. Judd Caulfield drives the net and pops Alex Killorn's feed up and over Woll.

As Aaron Cooney said, "Dad Strength" and the Ducks are back even. 3-3.

@SportingTrib | #FlyTogether

Flyers go back ahead shorthanded. That's a tough one.

Around a sliding Carlsson, Foerester whips one on net from a sharp angle, and Dostál just lets that one under the stick and pads to put Philly back in front, 3-2.

@SportingTrib | #FlyTogether

Ducks finally on the board, and it's Philadelphia's $18 million man Leo Carlsson. His first goal in five games and first 5-on-5 goal since the season opener.

2-1 Flyers, 11:22 P2.

@SportingTrib | #FlyTogether

Nick Jensen added to the scratches on the NHL Media Site.

That means Travis Mitchell is officially back in the Ducks blue line. Ducks are 4-1 with him, 0-5 without him. Maybe he was the secret sauce. 🤔

@SportingTrib | #FlyTogether

Nikita Klepov and Frank Vatrano are the healthy scratches for the Ducks in Philadelphia, per the NHL Media Site.

Lukáš Dostál is back in the starter's net.

@SportingTrib | #FlyTogether

Tonight's rosters from the NHL Media Site.

Pavel Mintyukov and Jeff Malott are out. Nick Jensen and Nikita Klepov are in. Judd Caulfield is still back in SoCal (birth of child).

@SportingTrib | #FlyTogether
